Rejected the family and documented the evidence in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1904.00563/REJECTED.md).

- Track A fails because Theorem 2 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.00563) gives a polynomial-time constructive route.
- The attempted Track B family passed generation, exact verification, corruption, scaling, canonicalization, and guess-resistance checks.
- Bare `easy` was hardened, but the structural hint enabled 2/3 oracle solves.
- After the single permitted escalation, Gemini also solved the hinted `medium` instance, failing mandatory gate G9(b).
- Measured at `medium`: Hopcroft–Karp used 3,136 operations on average; the compact cycle route required at most 213 operations.

No generator is being presented as shippable. The disposable oracle scratch directories were moved to `/tmp/1904_00563_scratch.uWRett`.
